I've ascended a [s] character with no reflection (Valk, Wishless,
didn't find any means of reflection (except the Nighthorn) until
midway through the ascention run).    The main things you've
got to worry about are lightning bolts. They can blow your
equipment even though you're resistant.  You can lose your
wands/rings this way.  Watch out for that ring of levitation on
Air and be careful with blue dragons/things holding
wand of lightning.

I've also played a Lethe patch game without permanent reflection
or drain resistance (monk), and just wore a SoR or wielded Stormbringer
when I saw the appropriate threat coming.  The main worry of lack of
drain resistance is gnolls with wands.  Normally you lose a level every
once in a while, you wield Stormy and you gain it back by killing the
creature that got you.  Esp. once you're at level 30, the extra XP
don't really matter.  With gnolls (chieftains), they can get in three
attacks without you having time to react - nasty!  Once you hit the
ascention run however, you've probably "collected" most of the
wands of draining available, and I would worry more about losing that
ring of slow digestion/whatever wands you have in your main inventory
than an experience level (don't forget that blessed full healing can
restore a drained level).

My advice would be that once you're ready for the run, you choose
reflection over drain resistance.  Better yet, go with your instincts
and drop the displacment for a CoMR.  In a choice between
reflection and displacement  - I'd go with reflection.

